descriptionMd:
Wikipedia and I talked about our love of the human parts of the Internet, and I pitched making Wikipedia feel this way for readers as an extension of my internet liveness work with [we were online](https://spencer.place/creation/we-were-online/) (WWO). I made a special experience on WWO that turned Wikipedia into a live, shared space. 
&nbsp;
With the extension installed, users can see other cursors on the same page, chat with them (with random usernames populated by Wikipedia articles), and follow people to go down rabbit holes together. In addition to these real-time interactions, the extension modifies Wikipedia to carry the traces of how people have browsed. For example, links grow colored patina from the colors of cursors clicking through, so you can see how people are exploring, and users can see their own cursor traces on different articles. 
&nbsp;
I made videos highlighting the work and the emotions for the Internet (and Wikipedia’s vision) that they aim to capture. 
&nbsp;
- [Video 1: Wikipedia self-portrait](https://www.instagram.com/reel/DXO_G66Dv0P/?hl=en)
- [Video 2: Browse Wikipedia together](https://www.instagram.com/p/DYpRnRAORbE/?utm_source=invited_by_Spencer_Chang)
- [More context](https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZBufc1NUjL/)
&nbsp;
Cumulatively, the videos have accrued >400k views across platforms.
